Description: Tools for analyzing and interpreting distributed lag nonlinear models (DLNMs) in epidemiological applications.
    Provides functions to simulate exposure scenarios, summarize lag-specific and period-specific effects,
    predict exposure-lag-response relationships, reduce multidimensional DLNM results, and perform sensitivity analyses.
    Supports both frequentist and Bayesian modeling approaches for environmental and plant disease epidemiology.
